{"agent_mode": null, "bash_calls": 5, "candidate_provenance": null, "checker_exit": 0, "checker_stderr": "", "checker_stdout": "round_money rounds half up; other helpers intact\nOBENCH_VERDICT: pass\n", "checker_workspace_files": {"pricing/__init__.py": {"bytes": 0, "mtime": 1791845574.119196, "sha256": "e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855"}, "pricing/money.py": {"bytes": 626, "mtime": 1791870494.055751, "sha256": "a9f94b05e50a7815d169e606b4f19987639fcfd3827966642c474b655d48126b"}, "tests/test_round_money.py": {"bytes": 385, "mtime": 1791870509.3127108, "sha256": "98c6e615bbdbcf986d50a1bd8b7636109b02adfb9b3759cc2efaecd463bcd8a6"}, "tests/test_split.py": {"bytes": 101, "mtime": 1791845574.119196, "sha256": "f21bbe9cf15cf7f51ff9f71318aca4794c29f5d66cb9ae2aa0d4c919043d9bcf"}}, "child_edit_calls": 0, "child_plan_reminder": false, "cmd": ["/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/27517f255bc0f6927f6358a38d2c34b2efe166af/omp", "-p", "`round_money(2.675)` returns `2.67` but customers expect `2.68`. Fix it.\n", "--mode", "json", "--provider", "vertex-anthropic", "--model", "claude-opus-5-5", "--yolo", "--session-dir", "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cap30-b2/aa38/omp-938/transcripts/with/trig-omp-bugfix-regress/1/session"], "completed": true, "dotnet_build_calls": 0, "edit_calls": 3, "ended_on_rejection": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "json", "final_workspace": "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cap30-b2/aa38/omp-938/cells/with/trig-omp-bugfix-regress/1/workspace", "fresh_subagents": 0, "harness": "omp", "harness_version": "omp/18.1.8 (/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/27517f255bc0f6927f6358a38d2c34b2efe166af/omp)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "My expected value in the VAT test was wrong: the product reprs as `2.675`, so it should round to 2.68. I'm replacing it with a direct case.\n`round_money(2.675)` now returns `2.68`.\n\n**Cause:** the float `2.675` is actually stored as `2.67499999\u2026`. Python's built-in `round()` (which the old code called) sees that stored value, so it went down. On top of that, `round()` breaks exact ties toward the even digit rather than up, which doesn't match the \"half up\" promise in the docstring.\n\n**Fix** (`pricing/money.py`): the function now turns the number into its shortest text form (`str(x)` gives `\"2.675\"`), rounds that as a `Decimal` to two places with `ROUND_HALF_UP`, and returns a float as before. `add_vat` calls `round_money`, so VAT amounts get the same behaviour. Negative amounts round away from zero, so `-2.675` becomes `-2.68`.\n\n**Tests:** I added `tests/test_round_money.py`, covering 2.675, 1.005, 0.125, 2.674, -2.675, and `add_vat`. pytest isn't installed here, so I ran the test functions directly with `python3`. They pass, and so does the existing `test_split`. My first VAT test case had the wrong expected value and failed; I replaced it with a direct case, which passes.\n\n`split()` has a similar float risk that I left alone: `int(total * 100)` cuts off the decimals instead of rounding, so for some totals `base` comes out one cent low. The final `round()` in that function covers it for the tested `10.00, 3` case.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 2, "replies_ok": 12, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 304327, "requests_cache_write": 44702, "requests_cost_usd": 0.3368194, "requests_count": 12, "requests_input_uncached": 26, "requests_output": 2617, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-bugfix-regress:claude-opus-5-5:trial1", "sampling_obser